      "title": "Module 06 — Security Fundamentals",
      "short": "M06: Security",
      "detail": "Why AI-generated code carries unique security risk. The eight patterns: SQL/command injection, hardcoded credentials, insecure deserialisation, path traversal, broken access control, missing validation, error disclosure. Prompt injection in daily coding: untrusted text, delimiter patterns, instruction hierarchy. Running and interpreting SAST tools: Semgrep, Snyk. Secrets scanning and pre-commit security gates. OWASP Top 10 applied to AI-generated code.",
